			"14": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SHAPE GENERATION\n\nAlright, enough of values, friction and noise, let's make us some shapes.\nThe whole patch runs on 100 instances of the circle node.\nWe use the Linear node to generate 100 sizes running from 0.01 to 0.02, just to give that little bit of variation.\n\nNext... Color! Let's move to the Color bit. Down.. Down.. Down.."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 435.82281494140625,
					"width": 1216.4853515625,
					"x": 310.467132568359375,
					"y": -460.706573486328125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ff2dc18a",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"15": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "COLOR\n\nWe see the return of the Choice In node, letting the user switch between Mono, Duo or Gradient.\nIn Mono mode we just use Color A for everything.\nIn Duo we use Color A and B. We join them to create a collection of 2 instances.\nWire will automatically repeat them to 100 instances in the Switch because we set the instance count of the Switch node to 100.\n\nIn Gradient mode we feed Color A and B into the Gradient Palette after which we shuffle the palette.\nThe reason for the shuffle is that we have the size of our circles running from 0.01 to 0.02.\nIf we just flat out run the gradient node over this, the smallest shapes  would be Color A and the biggest shapes would be color B, which just looks odd.\n\nWe've added an extra slider for color opacity. This value gets subtracted from the A(lpha) channel in the RGBA color."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 779.35748291015625,
					"width": 1317.21142578125,
					"x": 1008.061279296875,
					"y": 333.712493896484375
				},
