				],
				"name": "Texture Out"
			},
			"63": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "RENDER & FEEDBACK \n\nHere we are at our final stage, we render the shapes to textures before running it into a Video Mixer.\nWe feed the mixer back into itself to create feedback, nice trails of movement.\n\nThe Feedback float gets mapped from 0-1 to 0.99 with a big amount of skew.\nThis makes it so that the mapped value is skewed towards the end of the scale.\nThis is useful as a feedback range between 0 and 0.7 is barely noticable.\nMove the Feedback slider and hover over the Map nodes output to see this in action."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 569.8590087890625,
					"width": 860.85821533203125,
					"x": 2357.062744140625,
					"y": -458.862335205078125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"64": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MOVEMENT FUNDAMENTAL\n\nThe whole patch revolves around a single X\/Y position controlled by the Flock X and Flock Y parameters.\nLater we apply noise and friction to the X\/Y position, but that is completely optional.\nTry setting the Noise Min, Noise Max, Feedback and Friction parameters to 0 in the dashboard and you'll see that you end up with a single dot in space.\n\nWe use a Choice In node, renamed \"Control Mode\" to switch between the Manual, Sine and Perlin modes.\nIn manual mode the X and Y position is directly set by the Flock X and Y parameters, you  have manual control over the position of the flock.\nManual mode is nice in Arena\/Avenue as you can use envelopes to create unique movement patterns.\n\nIn Sine and Perlin mode the Flock parameters are used to modulate either a Sine oscillator or a Perlin Noise oscillator.\nIn addition to X and Y you also have control over the frequency of the oscillators. Frequency does nothing in manual mode.\n\nThe final node in the chain is an add node that combines the movement fundamental with the movement noise.\nAfter you're done playing with the fundamental, move over to the movement noise bit."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 1322.3380126953125,
					"width": 1866.0618896484375,
					"x": -1929.4051513671875,
					"y": -718.8807373046875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "fff26eb5",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"65": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MOTHERFLOCKER\n\nThis patch is a source that is meant to simulate flocking behavior.\nWe give the user control over the X\/Y position of the flock as well as control over how far and fast the individual dots deviate from the actual X\/Y position.\n\nThis patch nicely demonstrates how to combine randomness with user control.\n\nA basic understanding of instancing is required to follow along.\n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 204.774078369140625,
					"width": 571,
					"x": -1929.7430419921875,
					"y": -982.81488037109375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
